invariant: INV-17
file: src/gcm_avx512_ghash.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: start_powers loses always_inline, so clang and gcc compile it
  as a function of its own that each kernel calls, and the powers of the
  hash subkey it computes or copies lie in its frame, below the kernel's. lint-stack
  holds each frame under its ceiling on its own, so the two frames
  together can pass the GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN bytes the entry wipes: under
  gcc at -Og they did, by 64 bytes. Every byte the kernel writes is still
  right. The script requires that the kernel's object define no function
  beside the four and make no call.

--- old
static inline __attribute__((always_inline)) void
start_powers(gcm_avx512_powers *s, __m128i first_power, const uint8_t *stored, size_t top) {
--- new
static void start_powers(gcm_avx512_powers *s, __m128i first_power, const uint8_t *stored,
                         size_t top) {
